<title>FINLAND: FINNISH CO-OP BANKS 1996 PROFIT UP TO FIM 849 MLN.</title>
<headline>FINNISH CO-OP BANKS 1996 PROFIT UP TO FIM 849 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31-</p>
<p>				    (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit after credit losses	 849 vs 253</p>
<p> Loan and guarantee losses		    1,696 vs 2,200</p>
<p> Net income from financial operations     4,055 vs 4,579</p>
<p> Capital adequacy (BIS), percent	     11.7 vs 10.7</p>
<p> Income to expenses ratio			1.65 vs 1.63</p>
<p> Other income				     2,724 vs 2,230</p>
<p> Total income				     6,779 vs 6,809</p>
<p> Staff costs					1,962 vs 2,026</p>
<p> Other expenses				   2,140 vs 2,139</p>
<p> Total expenses				   4,102 vs 4,165</p>
<p>Net income before</p>
<p>  loan and guarantee losses		   2,677 vs 2,644</p>
<p> Write-downs on securities			132 vs 191</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures above cover the whole co-operative bank</p>
<p>group including its listed central bank OKOBANK .</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
